      <p class="mt-8 leading-8">

        A lemma is the form you would look up in a dictionary.

        Many different word forms may point to the same lemma.

      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border">

        <table class="w-full">

          <thead class="bg-slate-100">

          <tr>

            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-left">
              Surface Word
            </th>

            <th class="px-5 py-3 text-left">
              Lemma
            </th>

          </tr>

          </thead>

          <tbody class="divide-y">

          <tr>

            <td class="px-5 py-4 text-xl">
              كُتُب
            </td>

            <td class="px-5 py-4 text-xl">
              كِتَاب
            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td class="px-5 py-4 text-xl">
              كِتَابَيْنِ
            </td>

            <td class="px-5 py-4 text-xl">
              كِتَاب
            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td class="px-5 py-4 text-xl">
              الْكِتَابُ
            </td>

            <td class="px-5 py-4 text-xl">
              كِتَاب
            </td>

          </tr>

          </tbody>

        </table>

      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-slate-100 p-5">

        Think of a lemma as the "canonical" version of a word.
