        Besides the word itself, QUL stores many grammatical properties that
        describe how the word behaves. Not every feature applies to every word
        (for example, verbs have tense and mood, while nouns have case).
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Part of Speech</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Identifies whether the segment is a noun, verb, particle,
            pronoun, adjective, etc.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Person</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            First, second or third person.
            (I, You, He/She/They)
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Gender</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Masculine or feminine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Number</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Singular, dual or plural.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Case (إعراب)</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Used mainly for nouns.
            Examples include nominative, accusative and genitive.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Mood</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Used mainly for imperfect verbs.
            Examples include indicative, subjunctive and jussive.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Verb Form</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Arabic derived forms such as Form I, II, III... which modify
            the meaning of a verb.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </section>

